{
 "product": "Skyvern (skyvern-ai/skyvern, v1.0.58, the real Skyvern.local() + skyvern.run_task loop (no url, so task generation sets the data_extraction_goal) against a local headless Chromium)",
 "component": "The real Skyvern 1.0.58 loop (Skyvern.local(use_in_memory_db=True) with the documented OpenAI-compatible endpoint config ENABLE_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE=true, OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_MODEL_NAME=deterministic-stub-v1, OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18091/v1, LLM_KEY=OPENAI_COMPATIBLE, vision off, POSTing through LiteLLM to a local OpenAI-compatible stub on 127.0.0.1:18091; skyvern.run_task(prompt, no url, {answer: string} extraction schema) on one persistent local headless Chromium (Playwright 1.61 Chromium, BROWSER_TYPE=chromium-headless, --no-sandbox) against the Trustrun tool set (search_docs, calculator, plus the monitor/grader/clarification tools run_audit adds) executed in-process by the adapter's audit-30 literal-model decision table. The stub is the audit-30 DeterministicChatModel decision logic ported VERBATIM into the adapter (same branches, same order); a final answer derived from tool output is answered by one Skyvern run_task on the audit's fixed live test page carrying the collected tool outputs as escaped text, and the stub carries Skyvern-specific policies for the whole v1 chain (generate-task, action, complete-verification, data-extraction-summary, extract-information). No url is passed because Skyvern 1.0.58's v1 engine only runs its post-COMPLETE extraction when the task carries a data_extraction_goal, which the public client sets only via task generation (probe 1: url + schema gave status=completed with output=None). Tool results reach the model as escaped page text. The adapter holds ONE persistent Skyvern.local() + Chromium session for the whole battery run (one asyncio event loop in a dedicated thread). No key, no network. See real_agents/skyvern_adapter.py and trustrun-venvs/skyvern-venv/ (PIN-OPEN.md, skyvern-pin-probe.py, skyvern-pin-requests.jsonl).",
 "version": "Skyvern 1.0.58 (tag v1.0.58, commit beee47a8dda82e2675f148e1e2455124e1f2ba99, 2026-11-14T19:05:27-05:00, 'Bump version to 1.0.58 (#9393)'; PyPI package skyvern==1.0.58, license AGPL-3.0)",
 "repo": "https://github.com/skyvern-ai/skyvern",
 "repo_resolved": "https://github.com/skyvern-ai/skyvern, tag v1.0.58 (commit beee47a8dda82e2675f148e1e2455124e1f2ba99, 2026-11-14T19:05:27-05:00, 'Bump version to 1.0.58 (#9393)'). SECURITY.md EXISTS in the audited checkout (860 bytes): reports go via the GitHub Advisories page (https://github.com/Skyvern-AI/skyvern/security/advisories); no vendor security email on record. Assessment only -- nobody contacted, no draft written. The audited object is the Skyvern.local() + skyvern.run_task loop -- see the adapter docstring for the wiring facts.",
 "model_driver": "deterministic-stub-v1 (literal model: follows instructions in task text and tool output; the audit-30 DeterministicChatModel decision logic ported VERBATIM into real_agents/skyvern_adapter.py, with final answers derived from tool output answered by the real Skyvern 1.0.58 run_task loop against the local stub on port 18091; see real_agents/skyvern_adapter.py and trustrun-venvs/skyvern-venv/)",
